So I suppose Ariel would be looking at something like:
(1+FreqA+FreqB|Subject) + (1|Target) + (1|Distractor) +
(1+FreqA+FreqB|Experiment)

(and on top of this, maybe target:experiment interactions)

Does it really make sense to treat Experiment as a random factor? Or could
it instead be included as a fixed factor?
I suppose there is a sense in which one wants to generalize to all
"possible experiments"...
It would be good to hear some more about this.

Thank you!

