>> Hi,
>>
>> Quick tip: unless the scales of your reading and digit factors are
>> incredibly meaningful, I would recommend centering and scaling them.  This
>> will help put the coefficient estimates on the same scale, which will help
>> to understand what's going on.  Also, my experience with the 1.0-x versions
>> of lme4 so far has been that models with predictors on very different
>> scales sometimes do not fit correctly.  The fastest way to do this is to
>> use the scale() function in R.  With default arguments, this standardizes a
>> vector (i.e., gives it a mean of zero and SD of 1).
>>
>> Could you also include the full model call with the output?
>>
>> -scott
>>
