>>>> Two quick thoughts: (1) are there any correlations between A and B?
>>>>  Sometimes high degrees of collinearity in predictors can have this weird
>>>> sign-flipping effect. (2) from the last thing you said, it sounds like a
>>>> regular regression (avg over items) shows a very different pattern than the
>>>> mixed-effect regression  If so, then I would suggest carefully inspecting
>>>> the random effects for item, as well as simple counts of data points per
>>>> item, and whether there is any relationship between var A and B and the
>>>> item. You haven't mentioned what these variables are, or whether they might
>>>> be at least partially confounded with items (e.g., some values for var B
>>>> only occur in the context of some items).
